message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "R&D Alpha: Investment Intensity and Long-Term Stock Returns"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sehgal"
    given-names: "Abhishek"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9424-4695"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vastdreams/fse-rnd-alpha"
url: "https://research.finsoeasy.com"
abstract: >-
  Research platform and working paper investigating the relationship between
  R&D investment intensity and subsequent stock returns. Using an S&P 500
  large-cap universe (with index eligibility gated by addition dates) and
  July-June returns to mitigate look-ahead bias, the frozen publication
  snapshot reports an annual Q5-Q1 (HML_RD) premium of +3.84%/yr
  (Newey-West t = 1.78; win rate 71%) over Jul2001-Jun2025 (N=24 annual periods).
keywords:
  - R&D intensity
  - stock returns
  - factor investing
  - quantitative finance
  - innovation premium
  - long-horizon returns
